var TERMS_VERSION = "2026-10-v2";

// src/lib/termsTextEn.ts
var TERMS_TEXT_EN = `Only the Slovenian version of the terms is legally binding. This English text is a courtesy translation.
TERMS OF USE OF THE DRA\u017DBENIK.SI ONLINE PLATFORM
Version 2026-10-v2

1. GENERAL PROVISIONS
1.1 The dra\u017Ebenik.si platform (hereinafter: the platform) is operated by Dizain d.o.o., Karantanska ulica 28, 2000 Maribor, VAT ID SI57008060, registration number 9093494000, email info@drazbenik.si (hereinafter: the operator).
1.2 These terms govern the use of the platform and the relationships between the operator, sellers and buyers. By registering and using the platform, the user confirms that they have read and accept the terms.
1.3 The user must be at least 18 years old and have legal capacity. Companies and sole traders act as companies (business users), all others as private persons.

2. ROLE OF THE PLATFORM
2.1 The platform is an online marketplace that enables the publication of auctions, the placing of bids and the conclusion of sales contracts between seller and buyer.
2.2 The sales contract is concluded directly between the seller and the buyer at the moment the auction ends successfully. The operator is not the seller, buyer or owner of the items and is not a party to the sales contract.
2.3 The operator does not verify the accuracy, completeness and legality of item descriptions and does not guarantee the properties or legal status of items. The seller is responsible for the item, its description, properties and legality.
2.4 For each seller, the platform shows whether they act as a company or as a private person. Consumer rights (point 11) apply only when buying from a company.

3. REGISTRATION AND ACCOUNT
3.1 The user must provide true and complete data and keep it up to date. To take part in auctions, the user must confirm their email address and complete their profile.
3.2 The user is responsible for keeping their login credentials safe and for all activity on their account.
3.3 For security, fraud prevention or legal obligations, the operator may require additional identity verification, in particular when the user's total purchases in a calendar year exceed EUR 5,000.
3.4 The operator may temporarily restrict or close an account that violates these terms or the law. The operator informs the user of the reasons unless the law prohibits this.

4. AUCTIONS AND BIDS
4.1 Every bid placed is binding. A bid cannot be withdrawn or cancelled. This does not limit the statutory rights of consumers (point 11).
4.2 An auction ends when the published time expires. The bidder with the highest valid bid wins. If the winner does not pay within the deadline (48 hours), the seller alone decides how to proceed: the seller may offer the auction to the second-highest bidder at that bidder's bid (the price is shown before confirmation), republish it or delete it. Until the seller decides, nothing happens with the auction; the second bidder is notified of the offer by email and on the platform. The second bidder must accept the offer within 24 hours and, after accepting, has a further 24 hours to pay. If the second bidder does not accept or does not pay in time, the auction moves to the seller's unsold auctions, where the seller chooses how to proceed (republish or delete). The seller is notified by email and on the platform about an auction awaiting a decision.
4.3 The seller may not take part in auctions of their own items nor bid on them through other accounts to raise the price.
4.4 Items whose trade is prohibited or restricted by law, counterfeit items, items that infringe third-party rights and other items that the operator designates as prohibited are not allowed. The operator may remove a listing.
4.5 Display order: by default, auctions are shown by publication time (newest first); in the "Last chance" view by end time (those ending first come first); the carousel on the home page shows active auctions selected by end time. Users can narrow results with filters (region, category, handover method, condition, specifications) and by searching title or location. The seller's subscription package, the amount of the commission or any payment have no influence on the display order; there are no paid placements.

5. SELLERS
5.1 A seller may publish auctions once they have a confirmed email address, a completed profile and payouts set up with the payment provider (point 7).
5.2 The seller confirms that they will only offer items and services that comply with applicable law, that their description is truthful and that the item is their property or they may sell it.
5.3 After the auction ends and payment is received, the seller must ship or hand over the item to the buyer in accordance with the published handover method.
5.4 A seller acting as a company is responsible for fulfilling their legal obligations (consumer information, right of withdrawal, conformity of goods, tax obligations).
5.5 Because of legal obligations (in particular the Digital Services Act), the operator collects from sellers data on identity, address, contact, payment account and register entry and may request proof.

6. COMMISSION AND VAT
6.1 In addition to the price reached at the auction, the buyer pays the platform commission and VAT on the commission. The seller receives the full price reached at the auction.
6.2 The amount of the commission depends on the buyer's subscription package at the time of payment and on the price of the item, in accordance with the price list on the platform. The commission and VAT are shown before the bid is placed and before payment.
6.3 VAT on the commission is charged in accordance with applicable regulations. For buyers from Slovenia and private persons from EU countries, VAT is charged at 22%. For companies from another EU country with a valid VAT identification number (verified in the VIES system), the reverse charge applies. For buyers outside the EU, VAT is not charged.
6.4 The commission cannot be lower than the minimum commission of EUR 1.00. The commission is the operator's revenue. The operator issues the buyer an invoice for the commission.
6.5 Subscription packages: the paid packages Basic (EUR 20 per month) and Pro (EUR 50 per month) are paid in advance through the payment partner. The price includes 22% VAT, except where reverse charge applies under point 6.3 or no VAT is charged. The subscription renews automatically every month by charging the same payment method until the user cancels it in the Subscriptions section; cancellation stops automatic renewal, and the benefits of the package remain valid until the end of the period already paid. The invoice is sent to the user by email and is available on the platform.
6.6 For a subscription package, a consumer has the right to withdraw from the contract within 14 days of conclusion under the conditions laid down in the Consumer Protection Act (in particular for a service whose performance begins during the withdrawal period at the consumer's express request). Withdrawal is notified at info@drazbenik.si.

7. PAYMENT AND PAYOUT TO THE SELLER
7.1 Payments are processed by a payment service provider - the payment partner. Its terms apply to its use. The operator does not offer payment services and does not hold users' payment accounts.
7.2 The buyer pays the total amount (item price, commission and VAT on the commission) by card or bank transfer via the payment partner within the deadline stated upon winning. Non-payment is a breach of the terms (point 10).
7.3 The item price is booked on payment to the seller's account with the payment partner. The commission with VAT belongs to the operator.
7.4 The payout to the seller is held until receipt of the item is confirmed. The funds are released to the seller as soon as (a) the buyer confirms receipt on the platform, or (b) the seller enters the buyer's pick-up PIN code at a personal pick-up, or (c) the period under point 7.5 expires and the buyer has not filed a complaint.
7.5 If the buyer does not confirm receipt, the payout is released automatically: for shipment by post 7 days after dispatch (14 days for shipments abroad), for personal pick-up 7 days after payment, unless the buyer files a complaint within this period. Upon confirmation of receipt or entry of the pick-up code, the payout is released immediately without further waiting.
7.6 If the buyer files a complaint within this period, the payout is held until the dispute is resolved. The payout period allowed by the payment partner cannot exceed 90 days from payment; the operator therefore undertakes to resolve the dispute before this deadline.
7.7 The seller pays out released funds to their bank account on request in the settings (minimum EUR 10, at most one request per 24 hours). Funds that the seller does not request within 30 days of release are paid out automatically to their bank account. The operator bears the payout costs; the seller receives the full value of the item.
7.8 If the seller does not ship the item within 7 days of payment, the order is cancelled automatically and the buyer is refunded the full amount, including commission and VAT.

8. PICK-UP, DELIVERY AND CONFIRMATION OF RECEIPT
8.1 The handover method (personal pick-up or shipping) is determined by the seller when publishing the auction.
8.2 The buyer must confirm receipt of the item on the platform. At a personal pick-up, the buyer shows the seller the pick-up code only after inspecting the item; by revealing the code, the buyer confirms receipt.
8.3 If the item does not match the description, the buyer must file a complaint on the platform within the period that applies to holding the payout (point 7.5).
8.4 By confirming receipt on the platform or by revealing the pick-up code to the seller, the buyer declares that they have inspected the item, that it matches the description and all the seller's information, and that they accept it. With the confirmation, dealings on the platform between buyer and seller are concluded, the payout to the seller is released immediately and a complaint through the platform is no longer possible after confirmation. The same applies to personal pick-up and to shipping by post. The buyer should therefore confirm receipt only after inspecting the item. The statutory consumer rights under point 11 (when buying from a company) are not limited by this.
8.5 For sales above EUR 20, shipping with tracking is mandatory and the seller must enter the tracking number. For untracked shipments up to EUR 20, the seller bears the risk of loss and must enter the details of the posting receipt when marking the item as shipped.
8.6 The buyer may report a shipment as not received 4 days after dispatch (8 days for international shipments). The seller must provide proof of posting (post office receipt or a photo of the parcel) within 48 hours. If no proof is provided, the buyer is refunded in full and, for tracked shipments, the seller also receives a strike. If proof is provided, the operator decides the dispute; delivery cannot be proven for untracked shipments, so the decision is usually a refund to the buyer. The operator records the number of reports and disputes per user and may take action if abuse is suspected. A false dispatch declaration or an unfounded report is a breach of these terms.

9. DISPUTES AND REFUNDS
9.1 Buyer and seller first try to reach an agreement themselves via messages on the platform.
9.2 If no agreement is possible, either party may open a dispute. Based on the evidence submitted, the operator may decide that the payout is released to the seller or that the amount is refunded to the buyer. The decision does not exclude the parties' right to judicial protection.
9.3 If the amount is refunded to the buyer, the commission and VAT are also refunded and the operator issues a credit note.

10. NON-PAYMENT AND VIOLATIONS
10.1 Non-payment of the purchase price is a serious breach of the terms. A warning is given to the winner who does not pay for the auction in time and to the seller who cannot hand over a paid item. The second bidder receives no warning if they do not accept or if they decline the offer; they receive a warning only if they accept the offer and then do not pay in time. After the third warning, the operator may block the account.
10.2 The operator may temporarily or permanently close an account that violates the terms, or withhold payouts if there is a well-founded suspicion of fraud or breach of law. The user has the right to appeal to the support address (point 16.2).

11. CONSUMER RIGHTS
11.1 When the seller acts as a company and the buyer as a consumer, statutory consumer rights apply, in particular the right to information, conformity of goods and the right to withdraw from the contract within 14 days of receiving the goods, except in cases provided by law.
11.2 When the seller acts as a private person, consumer rights do not apply. The buyer buys the item as described. The seller is liable for conformity with the description and for defects they concealed, under the general provisions of the Code of Obligations.
11.3 The seller is responsible for implementing the right of withdrawal and the warranty.

12. INVOICES AND DOCUMENTS
12.1 The seller authorises the operator to issue, in the seller's name and on their behalf, an invoice or receipt for the sold item in accordance with the seller's status (private person or company, VAT payer or not). The seller is responsible for the accuracy of their data.
12.2 For sales between private persons, a purchase receipt without VAT is issued. The operator issues the commission invoice to the buyer.
12.3 Invoices and receipts are available to users on the platform and are sent by email.

13. TAX AND LEGAL OBLIGATIONS
13.1 As the platform operator, the operator is required to report to the Financial Administration of the Republic of Slovenia on sellers and their income (DAC7 Directive) if the seller completes 30 or more sales in a calendar year or their income exceeds EUR 2,000. The seller must provide the requested data, including the tax number, upon request.
13.2 The seller is responsible for paying taxes on their income.
13.3 If the user does not provide the requested data, the operator may withhold the publication of new auctions and payouts.

14. PERSONAL DATA
14.1 The operator processes personal data in accordance with the Privacy Policy. The data needed for payment and identity verification is also processed by the payment partner as an independent controller.
14.2 To carry out the transaction, the buyer and seller see the necessary data of the other party (name, delivery address).

15. LIABILITY
15.1 The operator is liable for damage only in the cases provided by law. The operator is not liable for outages of the payment partner, banks and other third parties, for the content of listings, for the actions of users and for the unavailability of the platform due to maintenance or force majeure.
15.2 The limitation of liability does not apply to intent, gross negligence and liability that cannot be excluded by law, in particular not in relation to consumers.

16. CONTENT, REPORTS AND COMPLAINTS
16.1 Anyone can report illegal content or a suspicious listing to info@drazbenik.si or via the form on the platform. We handle the report as soon as possible. If we remove a listing or restrict an account, we inform the user of the reason and of the possibility to appeal.
16.2 The user may file a complaint against a decision of the operator at info@drazbenik.si within 30 days of receiving the decision. We respond within a reasonable time.
16.3 Content and accounts are reviewed by the operator. Only the rules in point 10 (restriction of an account after non-payment) are applied automatically; at the user's request, a person at the operator reviews every decision.

17. CHANGES TO THE TERMS
17.1 The operator may change the terms. Users are informed of material changes on a durable medium (email or notice on the platform) at least 15 days before they take effect. During this period the user may terminate the contract free of charge and delete the account. To continue using the platform after the changes take effect, the user must accept the new version. For auctions that started before the change, the terms in force at the start of the auction apply.

18. FINAL PROVISIONS
18.1 The law of the Republic of Slovenia applies to relationships under these terms. For disputes with users who are not consumers, the court with subject-matter jurisdiction in Maribor is competent. For consumers, the statutory rules on jurisdiction apply.
18.2 If an individual provision is invalid, the other provisions remain in force.
18.3 The Slovenian version of the terms prevails.`;

